hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"116","Allāhumma-hdini fīman hadayt, wa ʿāfini fīman ʿafayt, wa tawallani fīman tawayt, wa bārik lī fīmā aʿṭayt, wa qinī sharra mā qaḍayt, fa-innaka taqdī wa lā yuqḍā ʿalayk, innahu lā yadhillu man wālayt, [wa lā yaʿizzu man ʿādayt], tabārakta Rabbanā wa taʿālayt.. O Allah, guide me among those You have granted guidance, grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, take care of me among those You have taken care of, bless me in what You have given me, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed, You decree and none can decree against him. Indeed, no one is humiliated whom You have befriended, [and no one is honored whom You have opposed]. Blessed are You, our Lord, and Exalted."
"117","Allāhumma innī aʿūdhu bi-riḍāka min sa-kaṭika, wa bi-muʿāfātika min ʿuqūbatika, wa aʿūdhu bika minka, lā uḥṣī thanāʿan ʿalayka, anta kamā athnayta ʿalā nafsik.. O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your displeasure, and in Your forgiveness from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You. I cannot enumerate praises upon You; You are as You have praised Yourself."
